    "description": "Apple just folded an iPhone in half, and the crease is almost invisible. 📱\n\nApple says the iPhone Duo's foldable display is a stack of layers held together by optically clear adhesives that let the layers glide as the screen folds, which reduces stress and the crease. Under the display are support ribs and a titanium panel, the hinge has more than 100 components, and a nano-texture finish minimizes how visible the crease is. It has a 5.4-inch outer display and a 7.6-inch inner display. Pre-orders start October 16 and it launches October 23.\n\nAnd proposals just got complicated. 👇\n\nSubscribe to Top Techs for more mind-blowing tech in under a minute.",
